  data: {
    LLM: 'Play Gnav with exact matador responses, fool side-rules, and token-elimination accounting. Stop swap loop immediately when Cuckoo appears.',
    Player: 'Gnav round: check your hidden piece, decide whether to stand or swap left, and manage matador outcomes to avoid finishing lowest.',
    objective: 'Avoid ending the round with the lowest piece and preserve your tokens while other players are eliminated.',
    gameplay: 'Play starts left of dealer and proceeds clockwise. On turn, a player either stands or tries to swap with the left neighbor. A normal neighbor must swap, but top five matadors change this. Cuckoo stops further swapping and triggers immediate reveal. Dragon and Katt refuse the swap and force the attacker to pay a token. Hest and Hus pass the attacker onward so they must try the next player instead. When play reaches dealer, dealer may exchange with the undealt stock with the same matador consequences; when a pass reaches dealer, draw replacement pieces until a non-pass value appears. At round end all reveal. Lowest value pays one token to pool; ties for lowest each pay.',
    keyRules: [
      'If dealt Narr (fool), you must signal it by knocking; at reveal both fool holder and next-lowest holder pay.',
      'If two fools are in play, both fool holders pay and may sit out the next round.',
      'Players who lose all tokens are eliminated; last remaining player wins the session.',
    ],
